What is here. These files are MiSTer-devel/Amstrad_MiSTer (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Amstrad_MiSTer), commit 6c2c39b (2026-06-03), copied
unchanged by tools/vendor_amstrad_mister.sh (SHA256SUMS lists them). The terms are the ones written in each file's header:

  GA40010/ga40010.sv, video.sv, casgen_sync.v, syncgen_sync.v   GPL v2 or later (Gyorgy Szombathelyi, 2020)   the Gate Array
  GA40010/rslatch.v                                             no licence text (the Gate Array's own latch cell)
  UM6845R.v, i8255.v                                            GPL v2 or later (Sorgelig, 2018)              the CRTC and the PPI
  color_mix.sv                                                  GPL v2+ (Sorgelig, 2018)                      the ink table
  Amstrad_MMU.v                                                 "(C) 2018 Sorgelig", CoreAmstrad r004, no licence text
  u765/u765.sv                                                  GPL v2 or later (Gyorgy Szombathelyi, 2017-2020) the FDC

The Z80 (T80pa) and the AY (YM2149) are the Spectrum core's (cores/zx/rtl, gen; BSD wording, T91 D2): shared, read through this core's core.toml, never
copied. The two files without licence text are kept as they came, with their credit lines. Not here,
on purpose: Amstrad.sv (the board top), Amstrad_motherboard.v (cores/cpc/trx/cpc_board.v is written from it and says so), hid.sv and the mouse
modules, crt_filter, sdram, tzxplayer, progressbar, playcity, dandanator, the MiSTer framework (sys/), and every ROM. The CPC's OS, BASIC and AMSDOS
ROMs are Amstrad's and never go into this repository, a bench, a package or a .cor: the app reads them at core start from the user's files
(roms: cpc os6128, basic6128, amsdos, os664, basic664, os464, basic464), the benches run programs written in the bench itself.

What is built is NOT only these files. cores/cpc/gen/u765.sv is what tools/cpc_gen.py makes of u765/u765.sv: one counted change (an initialiser that
depends on a function's arguments becomes an assignment per call, which Verilator needs and which is the authors' intent).

What the licence means here. GPL covers the gateware of this core and everything linked into its partial bitstream. A .cor or partial bitstream of
this core that is given to a third party has to come with its corresponding source: that is this directory (the upstream copy), cores/cpc/gen,
cores/cpc/trx, cores/cpc/layer2_cpc.v (our glue), the Spectrum core's files that this core reads (cores/zx/rtl, gen, shared), tools/vendor_amstrad_mister.sh,
tools/cpc_gen.py and tools/zxcpc_keys.py, and the build recipe cores/cpc/mono/build_mono.tcl - all of it is in this repository. The host (layer 1), the other cores and the applications are separate works in separate partial
bitstreams, link nothing of this core and are not covered; host/ is not part of this core's build.
